 "summary": "The public surface covers SN-A01\u2013A05, A07 and B01 with the characteristic API (bound by the operator norm, value on the zero map, one-sided ideal inequalities, Lipschitz bounds, continuity, homogeneity), reuses `singularValue` rather than adding a second `approximation` name, and needs no compatibility layer. I withdraw the earlier simp-annotation finding: each left-hand side has the bound variable `s` as head symbol and every lemma depends on `hs`, so global `@[simp]` is wrong and `simp [hs.smul]` is the right usage.",
